WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.400
- Is there a greater
meaning behind this mask,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.340
seen in the Halloween
display in the background

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.640
of the pharmacy in Halloween 4?

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:09.130
Maybe, just maybe.
(swooshing)

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.610
The last time on Things You Missed,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.810
we talked about the
strange, subversive secrets

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.320
that may change the way
you look at Halloween III.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.610
That movie, as unique as it
may be, was not well-received.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.320
It was the lowest-grossing
Halloween movie,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.020
and it did even worse with critics.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.140
For those in charge of
the IP, it was time to go

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.270
into damage control.
(bubbles popping)

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:28.350
The idea of making each movie
a unique standalone story

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.330
set on Halloween was abandoned in favor

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.830
of resurrecting Michael
Myers, but while the producers

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:34.930
wanted to forget about Season
of the Witch, the artists

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:38.440
behind Halloween 4 may have
felt a little bit differently.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.050
Take the school scene, for example.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:41.650
Now, this may be a total coincidence,

00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.860
but there are three doors
with Halloween decorations

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.260
in this set, and they are
the big Halloween three,

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.370
skeleton, witch and jack-o'-lantern.

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:49.970
We don't see the masks themselves,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.720
but we do curiously see
this exact combination

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.160
of Halloween avatars later
on at one of the houses

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.590
that Jamie trick-or-treats at.

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:58.740
That brings me to this
mask, which may look

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.220
a little bit familiar if
you've seen Halloween III.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.270
It almost seems to be
a zombie-like version

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.580
of the villainous
mask-maker, Conal Cochran.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.720
There may be another mask

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:08.830
that references Halloween
III, seen right here.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.150
You may remember one of the symptoms

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:10.983
of the microchip

00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:13.440
being distributed in the Silver
Shamrock masks was for bugs

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.690
and snakes to pour out
of the children's skulls.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.770
Of course, most of what
we see in Halloween 4

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:19.350
is designed to make us think more about

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.970
the initial two movies,
Halloween and Halloween II.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:22.803
To learn how the kills

00:01:22.803 --> 00:01:25.100
in this movie were inspired
from Michael Myers' past,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.845
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:27.845 --> 00:01:30.512
(intense music)

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.670
When writing Halloween II,
John Carpenter and Debra Hill

00:01:36.670 --> 00:01:38.680
made sure that Michael did not survive,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.040
because they felt they had creatively

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:41.530
exhausted the character and wanted

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.670
to open the door to
other Halloween stories.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.750
But, like their protagonist, Sam Loomis,

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.210
even they could not kill Michael Myers.

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:49.960
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.650
In this episode, we cover
The Return of Michael Myers.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.310
Literally, that's the name of the movie.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:57.310
Once again, I am joined by a guy I found

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.670
on the street who claims to have seen

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:01.430
a couple of Halloween
movies, Jimmy Champane.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.000
- Halloween sure is a
funny way to say Scream 3.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.590
- Over the years, there have
been a number of soft reboots,

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:08.810
like Halloween H20: 20 Years Later,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:11.580
and what I sometimes call Halloween H40.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.180
Looking back on Return, I'm tempted

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.390
to start calling it Halloween H10.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.150
Releasing and taking place
10 years after the original,

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.660
it tells a story very similar

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.260
to the initial Haddonfield murders,

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.510
but still technically more
of a sequel than a remake,

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.150
setting the standard for decade
anniversaries going forward.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.150
In fact, on this 10th anniversary,

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.850
the Michael Myers character
would be 31 years old.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.610
10/31 is Halloween.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:34.230
As a soft reboot, there are a lot

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.170
of parallels to Halloween (1978),

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:38.460
some of which were
situated very creatively.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.440
Let's get in to the things you missed.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.440
- I've only seen that
movie about 1000 times,

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:43.790
how could I not have noticed that?

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.814
(creepy music)
(blades slicing)

00:02:45.814 --> 00:02:48.147
(swooshing)

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.790
- We began on a rainy night
with a patient transfer,

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.530
not unlike the opening of the first movie.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.080
I do not know why they always choose

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.610
the day before Halloween to move him,

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.240
it never works out well for them.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.920
I imagine after 10 years of being

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.770
an invalid, the idea of Michael Myers

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.070
as an actual threat kind
of faded into legend

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:06.220
and the transfer personnel
let their guard down.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:08.300
- How many bodies did you find?

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.840
- [Policeman] It's hard to
tell, they're all chewed up.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.200
- What, so you can't count them?

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.510
- They also subtly let us
know that Laurie Strode,

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.570
the final girl from the past two movies,

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.490
was killed off-screen

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:18.530
by simply mentioning that Michael only has

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.760
one living relative, his niece, Jamie.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.790
Yeah, they kinda do Laurie dirty here.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.430
- I think only Alex
Browning could ever relate.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.960
- They do kind of honor Laurie though,

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.760
by naming Jamie after the
actress, Jamie Lee Curtis,

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.110
who, of course, played Laurie.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.180
Man, if you guys don't
know that Jamie Lee Curtis

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.260
played Laurie at this point in the series,

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:36.400
there's no helping you.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.290
- Jamie is supposed to be eight years old,

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.050
meaning that Laurie
must've given birth to her

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.120
pretty soon after escaping Michael Myers.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.000
She would've been no more
(baby crying)

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.570
than 19 when she had the baby.

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.780
On the bright side, I guess she got

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.370
over Ben Tramer pretty quick.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.990
- The next time someone tries
to tell you Halloween (2018)

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:52.180
didn't need to happen,
remind them that it brought

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.870
Ben Tramer back to life.
(angelic music)

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.210
- When we're first introduced
to Jamie, she's in her room,

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.800
having scary visions of
Michael coming after her.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.210
Only, we see Michael before she does,

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:03.130
which doesn't really make sense.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.110
If we, as the audience,
are seeing her visions,

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.650
we should only be able to
see the things that she sees.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.410
That's not why I brought
this scene up, though.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.560
On Jamie's door, I noticed
what I assume are some

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.220
of her drawings, such as this rendering

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.640
of a princess named Jessica
and a picture of a clown

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.886
named Clowny.

00:04:17.886 --> 00:04:19.860
♪ Never be creative again ♪

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.500
- This is a major clue about the lineage

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.780
of evil in her family.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.320
You'll recall that the
opening of Halloween

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.900
featured the six-year-old Michael Myers

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:28.500
wearing a clown costume and
stabbing his own sister.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:29.820
- I get what they were going for,

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.560
but I'm just gonna say it,
that was a lazy Easter egg.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.393
- Agreed.

00:04:33.393 --> 00:04:35.250
This clown drawing, her disturbing visions

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.120
and the fact that she
chooses a clown costume

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.770
for trick-or-treating are all clues

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.630
that she is doomed to the same fate.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.100
She ultimately stabs her stepmother

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:43.730
at the end of the movie and stands idly

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.900
in the same pose that her
uncle took 25 years prior.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.440
In each Halloween installment,
I've discussed what I see

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.070
as the main theme of each film,

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:53.080
what the director was
really trying to say.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.350
For Halloween 1, I talked
about how early exposure

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.040
to adult concepts can shape
a child's mind for the worse.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.010
In addition to that, while
it wasn't the main point

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.060
of that video, I also
talked about the idea

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.890
that Michael Myers represents
the personification of fate,

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.961
as discussed in Laurie's English class.

00:05:06.961 --> 00:05:09.040
(creepy music)

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:09.873
- [Teacher] That's right,

00:05:09.873 --> 00:05:12.810
Samuels definitely personified fate.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:16.800
In Samuels' writing, fate is
immovable, like a mountain.

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:20.340
It stands where man passes away.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:22.280
Fate never changes.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:23.740
- I think the concept of fate really

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:25.790
comes front and center in Halloween 4.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.850
Haddonfield was traumatized
by the murders in 1978.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.750
Everyone in town who's
old enough remembers it

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:32.330
and is willing to do just about anything

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.800
to prevent it from happening again.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.510
Even the new sheriff,
Meeker, who is stated

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:37.100
to never overreact about anything,

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.990
shuts down the town and imposes a curfew

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:40.950
before even having any proof that the big,

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.010
slow-walking man is back again.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.590
Mr. and Mrs. Carruthers have
a million emergency numbers

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:47.620
on their fridge, and the
men at the bar are willing

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:49.160
to take matters into their own hands

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.240
to protect the town from another disaster.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:53.320
- But, despite all of
this, the night plays out

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.860
almost exactly like it did 10 years prior.

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.320
Amy and Laurie were hired
to babysit Lindsey and Tommy

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.540
back in '78, and now
it's Rachel Carruthers

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.040
being forced to watch her
adoptive sister Jamie in 1988.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:06.380
Amy plans to bring over
her boyfriend, Paul.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.150
In Rachel's case, she
makes late-night plans

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.250
with a boy named Brady.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:10.690
Basically, they really played it safe

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:12.347
for Michael's big return
after Halloween III:

00:06:12.347 --> 00:06:15.470
Season of the Witch didn't
light the box office on fire.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.920
There's enough new stuff on the surface,

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.880
but at its core, it's a very similar movie

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:21.140
to Halloween, but just set 10 years later.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.920
And, obviously, I think that's exactly

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.800
what brought people back to the theater.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.450
- [Zac] In the original,
Michael gets his suit

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.670
from a mechanic that he took
out on the side of the road.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:30.280
This time, he visits an auto shop

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.150
and basically recreates his wardrobe.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:33.990
Jamie is bullied by the kids at her school

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.934
in almost the exact manner
that Tommy Doyle was.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:37.893
- Boogeyman, ooh, the boogeyman.

00:06:38.783 --> 00:06:41.592
- [Bullies] Boogeyman,
boogeyman, boogeyman!

00:06:41.592 --> 00:06:45.690
♪ Boogeyman, boogeyman,
Jamie's uncle's a boogeyman ♪

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:48.090
- While these details are
probably just evidence that

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.840
some things never change, it
is the kills in Halloween 4

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.060
that really cement the
idea that Michael Myers

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.953
terrorizing Haddonfield is
truly an inescapable fate.

00:06:56.953 --> 00:06:59.620
(intense music)

00:07:02.065 --> 00:07:04.648
(creepy music)

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.890
In the first Halloween,
we saw Michael attempt

00:07:07.890 --> 00:07:10.450
to recreate the horror he
had first created at age six,

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:12.450
using promiscuous teenage babysitters

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.890
as stand-in victims for his
sister, Judith, even going

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.560
so far as to arrange them
under his sister's tombstone.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.260
10 years after that, the kills now seem

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:21.910
to be recreations of
the night he came home.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:24.370
- For example, after Michael
arrives in Haddonfield,

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:26.150
his first victim there is a dog

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:29.310
in both the 1978 and 1988 versions.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:31.500
After Rachel and Jamie are
gathered by the police,

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.550
they take shelter in the sheriff's house.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:36.130
We only see the aftermath
of Deputy Logan's death,

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:38.610
but the sheriff's daughter,
Kelly, is taken out next.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.990
She and Brady would fill
the role of horny teens,

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:43.060
just like Bob and Lynda in the original.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:44.430
And, on top of that, her death is

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.640
kind of a combination of Lynda and Bob's.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.740
Remember, Bob was pinned
to the wall with a knife,

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.740
and then Michael pretended to
be Bob to get close to Lynda.

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:53.800
So, this time, things
are slightly changed.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.090
Michael sits in a rocking chair,

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:58.010
pretending to be Deputy
Logan, and he uses his shotgun

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.520
to impale Kelly and pin her into a door.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.230
Then, Brady is strangled, which happens

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:05.130
to be the same fate Annie and
Lynda suffered in Halloween.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.020
- Finally, there's a major
parallel in the final chase.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.080
Rachel fills the role of
Laurie Strode in this one,

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.630
as a responsible babysitter trying

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.190
to protect the kid that she's watching.

00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:14.660
We saw Laurie hide in a closet

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.650
and use a coat hanger to
poke out Michael's eye

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.820
and temporarily blind him in Halloween 1.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:21.190
Then, in Halloween II, she
shoots him in the eyes,

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.930
or I guess just slightly above the eyes?

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:26.249
But the drip down once again
renders him unable to see.

00:08:26.249 --> 00:08:28.840
(blade swiping)

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.673
Or apparently use any kind
of critical thinking at all.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.710
Rachel, who is stated to have been babysat

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.230
by Laurie when she was younger...

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:39.848
- Your mother used to babysit
me when I was your age.

00:08:39.848 --> 00:08:40.900
I bet you didn't know that.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:42.470
- Apparently picked up
a thing or two from her,

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.930
because she saves the day at the school

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:46.060
by blinding Michael with
a fire extinguisher,

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.200
which leads to this hilarious interaction.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.820
- In the school!
(banging on truck)

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:50.850
- Pull over, Earl!
(alarm ringing)

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:52.490
- We heard the alarm.
- [Rachel] He's inside!

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:54.300
- [Earl] Jesus, where?
- [Rachel] In the school!

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.910
- There are other
similarities to 1978 as well.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.710
For example, we see other teens
dressed up as Michael Myers.

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:01.830
- [Sheriff Meeker] Is that him?

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:02.780
Is that him?

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:03.613
- [Loomis] Yes.

00:09:03.613 --> 00:09:04.446
- What?

00:09:04.446 --> 00:09:05.279
What do you mean, yes?

00:09:05.279 --> 00:09:07.070
I mean, you think he'd be a
little bit more apprehensive

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.580
after the whole Ben Tramer
incident, where an innocent kid

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.290
in a Michael mask ended up getting killed.

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.840
Actually, history does
kind of repeat itself here.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:15.640
Our good, old Illinois boys are concerned

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.190
when they hear about the curfew and decide

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:19.710
to take matters into their own hands.

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:22.543
(gunshots firing)

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.740
And, it turns out they shot
someone named Ted Hollister.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:30.212
Poor Ted Hollister, we
never even saw your face.

00:09:30.212 --> 00:09:32.760
(sobs) And now you're gone.
(somber music)

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.200
- Damn, man.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.800
- Then, later that night,
after murdering someone,

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.720
they fire their guns in
the air while driving

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.280
past the police officers on
their way into Haddonfield,

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:44.130
where a serial killer is
currently on the loose.

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:46.100
I wanna like these
good, old Illinois boys,

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:48.110
but they're just not very smart.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:50.500
It's no wonder most of them
get taken out by Michael.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.000
However, that does lead
to Rachel getting control

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.650
of their truck and ramming
it in to her masked stalker.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.190
And, just like Halloween 1,
there's that fake-out moment

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.160
where he appears to be
dead and then rises up,

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.720
using the same sit-up motion.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.940
Then, at the end, when
Michael is seemingly defeated

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.800
for good (like, at least for this movie)

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.230
we see that Jamie still
can't change her fate,

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.230
because the evil seems
to be passed down to her

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:12.550
and we see her point of view
as she puts on the clown mask

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.900
and stabs her (step)mother, a
scene that Loomis recognized

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.500
as being identical to
Michael's attack on his sister.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.840
- So, while we don't have
a long in-class lecture

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.100
about fate this time around,
the idea of immovable fate

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.150
is the driving force behind
the events of Halloween 4.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:28.360
We even have this overly
religious reverend,

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:31.060
who Dr. Loomis catches a
ride into Haddonfield with.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.730
I mean, he specifically says
that you can't kill damnation

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.650
because it doesn't die like a man does,

00:10:35.650 --> 00:10:38.860
and next that the apocalypse
always has a name and a face.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.280
- Well, in this case, that name is Michael

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.800
and that face is William Shatner,

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.520
looking decidedly more surprised

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:48.280
than he does in earlier
installments in this franchise.

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.800
- There's also the dog named Sundae.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:51.790
Sunday is the holy day in Christianity

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.940
and Michael is made out
to be the spawn of Hell.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:57.001
Even the security guard at the
hospital seems to think so.

00:10:57.001 --> 00:10:59.386
- Jesus ain't got nothin'
to do with this place.

00:10:59.386 --> 00:11:00.505
Welcome to Hell.

00:11:00.505 --> 00:11:01.860
- [Zac] So, it seems
like the reverend may be

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:04.310
onto something with his
apocalyptic provisions.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:06.950
Then again, that reverend
also says things like...

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:09.810
- I saw it, clear as breasts
and blue suede shoes.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:11.740
- Do you have any idea
what that means, Jimmy?

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:13.200
- No, I don't.

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:14.780
- Yeah, he's also DUI.

00:11:14.780 --> 00:11:16.330
That's a pretty serious crime

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.120
and it goes completely unaddressed,

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:19.580
as does the fact that this diner

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.330
is just filled with pictures
of regular Abraham Lincoln.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.180
I wanna take a closer look at the costumes

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:26.130
of some of Jamie's
classmates at the school.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:27.630
This kid in particular wears a getup

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:29.150
from the '80s cartoon M.A.S.K.

00:11:29.150 --> 00:11:31.100
and it has a red truck with an explosion.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:33.190
It almost seems to be a
reference to Michael Myers,

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.790
who, of course, wears a
mask and steals a red truck,

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.330
which causes an explosion.

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:38.780
I'm guessing that explosion is also

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:39.980
why the phone lines are down later,

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:42.160
and this image almost
looks like a burning cross.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.670
Maybe a symbol for the Judgment Day

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:44.620
mentioned by the reverend.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:47.380
- [Reverend Sayer] I ain't
got 'til Judgment Day!

00:11:47.380 --> 00:11:49.190
When Jamie is picking out her own costume,

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.090
she browses through all
of the other costumes

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:53.990
worn by her classmates before
settling on her clown suit.

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:55.340
This essentially says that she cares

00:11:55.340 --> 00:11:57.300
more about doing her own
thing than fitting in

00:11:57.300 --> 00:11:59.050
with the other classmates,
which I think ties

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:00.920
into the idea that I
keep on talking about,

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:03.180
that nothing can sway
her from her own destiny.

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:04.940
Interestingly, the kid who compliments her

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.300
is the same kid who was bullying

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:07.550
the **** out of her at school.

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:10.450
So, she kind of ends up fitting
in just by being herself,

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:13.050
or, you know, the costume
budget was really low.

00:12:13.050 --> 00:12:14.390
- After picking out her costume,

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:16.440
Jamie is scared by an
encounter with Michael.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:18.210
There's actually a clue that
he's going to be in there

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.580
when they first pull up and you see

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:22.340
the big industrial hook on
the truck across the street.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.320
If you paid close attention,
you'll remember it from

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.220
when Dr. Loomis explored the
auto shop earlier in the movie.

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.290
Also, the girl who drops
Rachel and Jamie off

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.010
at the drug store is named Lindsey.

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:33.010
I'm pretty sure that's
grown-up Lindsey Wallace,

00:12:33.010 --> 00:12:35.210
the little girl who
survives the first movie.

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.860
- Anyway, back on topic.

00:12:36.860 --> 00:12:38.970
When Michael scares Jamie
in the costume area,

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:40.900
she screams and Rachel comes running

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.650
and just intentionally knocks
over the sticker display.

00:12:44.953 --> 00:12:46.000
(crashing)
Why did she do that?

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.810
I mean, look at this, play
it back, you just see her

00:12:47.810 --> 00:12:50.270
clearly go out of her way
to knock this thing over.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:53.011
- It's very reminiscent
of this beautiful moment.

00:12:53.011 --> 00:12:54.402
(wheels screeching)

00:12:54.402 --> 00:12:55.235
- [Policeman] I couldn't stop.

00:12:55.235 --> 00:12:56.610
- And then, why do they not just look

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:58.300
right across the store and see Michael?

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:00.160
This whole scene makes no sense.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.610
I mean, I know I already massacred

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:03.000
our good, old Illinois boys,

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:06.232
but I think Rachel is maybe
also not the smartest.

00:13:06.232 --> 00:13:08.614
- [Brady] Ah, metal,
god damn it, it's metal!

00:13:08.614 --> 00:13:09.730
- [Rachel] What does that mean?

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:11.770
- You don't know what metal is?

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:15.570
You know, like, solid
material, strong, shiny,

00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:17.026
conducts electricity.
(electric crackling)

00:13:17.026 --> 00:13:18.530
(sighs) There's no hope for you, is there?

00:13:18.530 --> 00:13:21.240
Anyway, I think that's just
about it for Halloween 4,

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:22.590
unless you have anything to add.

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:24.370
- There is this one
part where, when Rachel

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.650
is at Chief Meeker's
house, she comes downstairs

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:28.570
to talk to Deputy Logan, and if you look

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.560
in the background,
Michael pops his head out.

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:32.070
You might've missed that, so we'll tack it

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:33.420
on there, just in case.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:34.600
- Next time, we'll move on

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:38.000
to Halloween 5: The
Revenge of Michael Myers,

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.420
a somehow even more generic title.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.130
- You see, life after Halloween 4

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:43.870
wasn't exactly smooth sailing.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:46.240
- We're four videos into
this Halloween collaboration,

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:48.080
so if you haven't subscribed to Jimmy yet,

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:49.160
I don't even know what you're doing.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:51.370
For my full collection
of Halloween analyses,

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:53.030
click that playlist on the left,

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:54.870
and if you love all things Halloween,

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.920
make sure you subscribe to CZsWorld.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.450
I've got new horrors every week,

00:13:58.450 --> 00:13:59.540
so ring the death bell

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.820
and select all notifications
